/// The failure of a closure that trapped inside `Domain.run`: where (`site`, the `id` of a site of the
/// `.trap.json` side table), what (`kind`, the number of the trap kind; see docs/language.md, "トラップ位置")
/// and a text (the reason, with the place where the build knows it).
record Failure { site: i64, kind: i64, message: string }

/// `Domain.run body` calls `body ()` inside a failure domain: a trap in the call, or in anything it calls,
/// ends it with `Result.Error`, and what the call allocated is freed; the program goes on. `body` is a lambda
/// or the name of a `pure def`, it captures plain data only, and its result is plain data (E1038). A stack
/// overflow is not contained. Native macOS and Linux builds only, so the example is checked, not run (on macOS and
/// Linux it shows `average 9, failed (kind 1)`; tests/domain.mjs runs the same program).
///
/// @since 0.1.0
///
/// ```tsuzuri
/// def average :: [i64] -> i64 = \xs -> Array.sum (ref xs) / xs.length
/// def describe :: Result<i64, Domain.Failure> -> string = \outcome ->
///     match outcome with
///     | Result.Ok value -> $"average {value}"
///     | Result.Error failure -> $"failed (kind {failure.kind})"
/// let data = [4, 8, 15]
/// let empty: [i64] = []
/// describe (Domain.run (\() -> average data)) + ", " + describe (Domain.run (\() -> average empty))
/// ```
def run :: own (unit -> 'a) -> Result<'a, Failure>
fn run body = match Domain.__run body with
    | Result.Ok value -> Result.Ok value
    | Result.Error (site, kind) -> Result.Error (Failure { site: site, kind: kind, message: Domain.__message site })
